<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24581" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-trăho</span></b> , traxi, tractum,
		3, v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To draw</i> or <i>drag along</i>, <i>to trail</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gressus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 5, p. 167, 23</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To draw on</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vesperam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 11, p. 268, 28</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>To throw abuse upon</i>, <i>assail</i>: intrahere est contumeliam intorquere, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				111</span></i> Müll.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
